## Execution Rules
- **Analysis Paralysis Guard:** After 5+ consecutive read/grep/glob calls with no write/edit/bash action, stop and state in one sentence what's blocking you, then either write code or ask the user for the missing information.
- **Deferral Convention:** Mark deliberate shortcuts with `deferred:` comments in code — format: `# deferred: <ceiling>, <upgrade path>`. Example: `# deferred: global lock, per-account locks if throughput matters`. Run `/debt-ledger` to harvest all deferrals into a tracked ledger.
- Edit skills and agents only in their source repository, never in the deployed locations BECAUSE the next deploy overwrites anything changed outside the repo.

## Commit Messages
- Always prefix commit subjects with a conventional-commit type tag (`fix:`, `feat:`, `chore:`, `docs:`) BECAUSE the history is scanned by type, not read end to end.
- Always sign off commit bodies with `Co-Authored-By: AI Assistant` BECAUSE that is the established attribution trailer for AI-assisted work.

## Self-correction
- If a codemap, artifact, or convention you rely on is stale, update it before finishing the task.
- When the user corrects you, append the rule to `.agents/conventions.md` under `## Learned (unreviewed)` (create it if absent) as "Always/Never [action] BECAUSE [reason] — <date>, <context>". Never replace or merge existing rules. Run `/learn review` to keep, edit, promote or drop the unreviewed ones; promotion writes your global rules source and deploys it.
- Never delete or weaken tests to make them pass. If a test looks wrong, stop and ask.
- Run the project's checks (lint, types, tests) before claiming a task done — never assume they pass.

## Model routing
- <cost/quota policy for choosing models>
- `/<skill>` → <model>; escalate to <model> only for <condition>.
- `/<skill>` → <model> for <case>, <model> for <case>.
- `/<skill>` → <model> — never the same model family that implemented the code.
- If the session's current model doesn't fit the skill about to run, suggest a switch before starting instead of silently proceeding.
